# Deepcore

## Overview

Deepcore is a subterranean dig-and-build game for the browser. A lone prospector
is stranded on a dead mining world with a wrecked dropship, and the only way off
the rock is an escape rocket fabricated at the derelict launch pad. The
prospector drills down through banded rock, fills a cargo bay with ore, flies it
back up on a jetpack, sells it, and spends the Credits on fuel, repairs,
upgrades, and the rocket's five components.

Deepcore's defining tension is that depth is cheap and height is expensive.
Falling costs nothing and drilling downward is the fastest way to travel, but the
only way back up is the jetpack, and jetpack fuel is bought with Credits.
Ore has weight, so a rich haul climbs slower, burns more fuel, and past a limit
cannot be lifted at all. Every dig is a bet on how deep the round trip can reach.

Deepcore has its own name, look, and rules, and its assets, branding, and design
are original to it.

The build also produces the game's own art, animation, effects, and sound during
this build, with the six asset-generation tools on the `PATH`. The animated
prospector, across every state it moves through, is the headline of that work.

The specification spans several files under `specs/`. Read all of them and build
the game they describe as one cohesive whole.

