## The runtime

This game stands on no engine, so the runtime under it is yours to write: the
frame loop and the delta time it measures, the canvas fit, keyboard input, audio,
asset loading, and the debug overlay. Where this specification speaks of the
runtime it means that layer, and it states only what Deepcore needs from it. How
the layer is structured is yours to decide.

The mine is larger than the viewport, so the camera that scrolls the view over it
is part of the game and part of what you write.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
## The runtime

The game is built on the {{engine.name}} engine, which documents itself in the
`engine/` directory at the root of this repository. It owns the frame loop and
the delta time the game is given, input actions, audio cues, asset loading, the
canvas fit, and the debug overlay. Read its documentation before you start. This
specification states only what is specific to Deepcore.

The engine draws nothing and holds no camera: it hands the game a 2D drawing
context covering the logical stage. The mine is larger than that stage, so the
camera that scrolls the view over it is part of the game, applied as the game's
own transform on that context.
